kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[1]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  add_requirement,ar17,"react-loop-continues-after-tool-call","The ReAct loop MUST continue to a next model round after executing tool calls (feeding the tool results back into history), and MUST terminate a turn only when a model round produces NO tool call (tool_calls is empty). The loop MUST NOT terminate merely because the model stream emitted XyChunk::Done: providers send Done at the end of every single model stream including ones that contain FunctionCalls (openai yields FunctionCall then Done at finish_reason; anthropic and openai-responses likewise), so treating Done as turn-end aborts every tool-calling turn after one round and the model never sees the tool results. Evidence: react.rs had if done { break } after TurnEnd where done was set by XyChunk::Done, so a tool call (FunctionCall followed by Done) broke the for-loop before the continuation round; a stateful mock model test confirmed the continuation text never reached the caller; the correct termination tool_calls.is_empty() already existed at react.rs:356.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[2]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  ar17,"tool-call-then-continuation","a model round emits a FunctionCall then Done and the agent executes the tool","the loop processes the tool result and calls the model again","the model continuation round (a final text reply with no tool call) reaches the caller and the turn ends with that reply visible"
  ar17,"plain-text-turn-unchanged","a model round emits only text and no tool call then Done","the loop terminates after that single round","the turn ends after one round with no spurious continuation (the fix does not change plain-text behavior)"
